    48	## 1. Langfuse API via CLI
    49	
    50	Use the `langfuse-cli` to interact with the full Langfuse REST API from the command line. Run via npx (no install required):
    51	
    52	Start by discovering the schema and available arguments:
    53	
    54	```bash
    55	# Discover all available resources
    56	npx langfuse-cli api __schema
    57	
    58	# List actions for a resource
    59	npx langfuse-cli api <resource> --help
    60	
    61	# Show args/options for a specific action
    62	npx langfuse-cli api <resource> <action> --help
    63	```
    64	
    65	### Credentials
    66	
    67	Set environment variables before making calls:
    68	
    69	```bash
    70	export LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-...
    71	export LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-...
    72	export LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com # example for EU cloud. For US cloud it's us.cloud.langfuse.com, and can also be a self-hosted URL. The server must always be specified in order to access Langfuse.
    73	```
    74	If `LANGFUSE_BASE_URL` is used instead of `LANGFUSE_HOST`, run `export LANGFUSE_HOST="$LANGFUSE_BASE_URL"`.
    75	If not set, ask the user to set them in their shell or a `.env` file. Keys are found in the Langfuse project under Settings -> API Keys; the user should create a project API key pair there. If they do not have a Langfuse account yet, share that they can create one for free at `https://langfuse.com/cloud`. Do not ask them to paste keys into chat for security reasons.
